{%- comment -%}
  Obfuscated email link. The address is base64-encoded at render time; the real
  mailto: href and visible text are assembled client-side by the decoder in
  layout/theme.liquid, so scraper bots never find a plain address in the raw HTML.
  Falls back to the contact page when JS is disabled.

  Accepts:
    email (required) - address to obfuscate
    class (optional) - extra class(es) for the <a>
    label (optional) - visible fallback text shown before JS runs (default: "Email us")
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if email != blank -%}<a class="obf-email{% if class != blank %} {{ class }}{% endif %}" data-e="{{ email | strip | base64_encode }}" href="{{ pages.contact.url | default: '/pages/contact' }}" rel="nofollow">{{ label | default: 'Email us' }}</a>{%- endif -%}
